  "paper_id": "ccs-2024-petal-ensuring-access-control-integrity-against-data-onl-5b19ff8c",
  "title": "PeTAL: Ensuring Access Control Integrity against Data-only Attacks on Linux",
  "abstract": "Data-only attacks are emerging as a new threat to the security of modern operating systems. As a typical data-only attack, memory corruption attacks can compromise the integrity of kernel data, which effectively breaks the premises of access control systems. Unfortunately, the prevalence of memory corruption vulnerabilities allows attackers to exploit them and bypass access control mechanisms. Given the arbitrary memory access capability, attackers can overwrite access control policies or illegally access the kernel resources protected by the access control systems.",
